  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (the tail of an unnamed BS IT specialization, this BS IT IoT specialization, and the Doctor of Information Technology); this ledger assumes the BS in Information Technology, Software Development in an Internet of Things Space was intended.",
    "The 33-credit general education block is derived rather than printed: the capture states 45 general education quarter credits and lists MAT1050 and MAT2051 (12 credits) as required courses. It is assumed these count within the 45. This assumption is consistent with the 180 total (45+54+36+33+12).",
    "The capture does not state whether MAT1050 and MAT2051 satisfy the 4-quarter-credit minimum for the Natural Science and Mathematics category.",
    "Individual general education course credits on page 148 are garbled by the two-column layout and cannot be reliably paired with course codes.",
    "The capture requires a minimum of 54 quarter credits from the 3000-level and above. It does not show how the listed courses plus electives satisfy this.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit (must-complete-at-Capella) policy is stated in the capture, so all requirements are marked institutionalOnly false.",
    "The optional Honors Pathway (PHI-H2005 3, COM-H4005 6, SOC-H3005 6; at least 15 quarter credits applied toward general education) is not included as a required line item.",
    "Course prerequisites are referenced but not listed in the capture.",
    "Requirements for the FlexPath (program points) option are not mapped for this program."
